# .secretscan-deny — example / template.
#
# scripts/check_no_secrets.py reads a file at the repo root named exactly
# ".secretscan-deny" (no ".example" suffix) and flags any line, in any
# tracked text file or recent commit message, that contains one of its terms
# (case-insensitively). Copy this file to ".secretscan-deny" and fill in your
# own internal names — that real file is gitignored (see .gitignore) so the
# deny-list itself is never a public artifact.
#
# Format:
#   - One lowercase term per line.
#   - Lines starting with "#" are comments and are ignored.
#   - Blank lines are ignored.
#   - Matching is a plain case-insensitive substring search, not a regex.
#
# Typical entries: an internal codename, a private project or org name, an
# unreleased product name, an internal hostname — anything that should never
# leak into a public commit, file, or deployed Space, but that the built-in
# token/absolute-path patterns in check_no_secrets.py would not catch.
#
# Example (commented out — this file ships with no real terms):
# my-internal-codename
# some-private-project-name
